I've gotten _enormously_ better at nethack since I started playing 
random char protection rackets.
I can get >70% of random chars, and >80% of tourists down to minetown
at xl1 with enough gold to buy down to AC1 and a bit of change for
clairvoyance.

The keys - as I see them.

NETHACK IS NOT QUAKE. Play slowly.

Kill no monsters at all - if possible you want to be able to kill and
eat that floating eye that pops up.
If you have potions of healing that will raise your HP significantly,
quaff them first turn. Gives rock trap resistance.

In almost all cases, wear all (pet tested) armour you can.
You are not a caster, you're a tank.
Check _all_ armour to see if it's better than what you're wearing.
Elbereth - finger E - is a vital skill, finger-E several times till you
get at least 3 or 4 down correctly. (:)
Put E down before you go down stairs, if you need to come back up to
heal, you don't want stuff attacking you.
Learn to let your pet explore new areas - and how to keep it following 
well - stay close to it, and keep it fed.
You should - if you don't have piles of food - never pray for hp, run
away!
Dark mines levels are a problem, I find that E'ng the stairs, maybe
exploring the nearest 8 squares to give you an idea of terrain, then 
picking up any missiles that are thrown at you, and taking stuff
upstairs to dump and heal, works well.
Then once the noises stop - carefully explore while keeping near your
pet.
You do not have to kill (or have your pet kill) everything. If you can
run past a level in the mines, do so, unless it's safe to kill
everything, and take their stuff.

Go down the normal branch credit cloning all the shops, till you get to
4000 gold or so. Trying to credit clone in minetown is often suicide -
there are too many chokepoints.
Map your retreat - opening all doors is usually a plus - if you've got a
monster closely following you, you don't want to have to stop and open
doors.




